      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": {"en": "Tener for sensations, estar for feelings"},
      "texto": {
        "en": "What your body feels is a noun with **tener**: tengo **hambre**, **sed**, **sueño**, **frío**, **calor**, **miedo**, **prisa**.\n\nBecause they are nouns, very is **mucho** or **mucha**, never muy: tengo **mucha** hambre, **mucha** sed, **mucho** sueño, **mucho** frío.\n\n**Tener ganas de** + infinitive is to feel like: no tengo ganas de salir.\n\nYour mood is an adjective with **estar**, and it agrees with you: estoy **cansado** / **cansada**, **triste**, **contento**, **enfadado**, **nervioso**, **preocupado**.\n\nThree kinds of cold: **hace frío** (the weather), **tengo frío** (me), **está frío** (the coffee)."
      }
    },
